+# A same-year original confirms an audit-context 8000.1C citation; the 9/11 case outcome remains missing
+
+October 29, 2026, America/New_York. B129 / PD01–PD04. The previously unacquired FAA FY 2006 Performance and Accountability Report has now been preserved and selected pages visually read. Its reproduced **November 14, 2006 OIG memorandum, QC-2007-009**, expressly places corrective-action follow-up under **DOT Order 8000.1C**. This advances a specific same-year policy-context source. It does not establish the operative investigation provisions or completed action on **CC-2006-085 / 042R0122001**.
+
+## Exact source, scope and the newly verified passage
+
+The [official FAA PDF](https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/about/plans_reports/archive/Combined_FY_2006_FAA_PAR_Final_v6_12-14-2006.pdf) contains **181 physical pages**, **6,404,033 bytes**, SHA-256 **ebd9c3ff368cbf69d971f4eaf88466570b63d64b8989cdc3779108ee144f90af**. The acquisition is October 30 UTC / October 29 in America/New_York; those are two representations of the same recorded access instant, not competing acquisition events. Original bytes remain unchanged on verified media; raw pages and signatures are excluded from this public addition.
+
+The relevant memorandum occupies **physical pp. 105–106 / printed report pp. 94–95 / memorandum pp. 1–2**:
+
+- **Physical p. 105, subject/date/report-number fields and opening paragraph:** the memorandum is dated November 14, 2006, report **QC-2007-009**, and concerns quality-control review of KPMG's audited FAA financial statements for FY 2006 and FY 2005. Preserve the report's fiscal-year title, memorandum number and actual displayed date separately; this is not the 9/11 communications investigation report.
+- **Physical p. 106, paragraph beginning with KPMG's 28 recommendations:** OIG agrees with those recommendations and makes no additional ones; it records FAA concurrence, agreement and a commitment to corrective actions during **FY 2007**. The same paragraph cites **DOT Order 8000.1C** and states that corrective actions responding to the recommendations are subject to follow-up.
+
+The passage demonstrates an actual late-2006 OIG use of that order number in an FAA **financial-audit** setting. It does not establish that every provision of the held 1989 order was unchanged in 2006, identify an FAA implementing amendment, or prove that Chapter I audit procedures governed the separate Chapter II investigation. An agreement or future commitment in this memorandum is not a completed implementation or an investigative personnel decision.
+
+## Preserve the prior policy/version observations
+
+The [earlier directive crosswalk](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/f3a71187146eec653eab636f1e24cd1df25f4c4e/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-directive-crosswalk-2026-10-29/README.md) remains unchanged. It preserved the checklist's 8000.1 c → 2900.1 implementation link, its displayed **7/5/85** date, the held 8000.1C cover's **7-20-89** date, FAA 2970.3's explicit **8000.1A Chapter I** purpose wording, and the differing **ABU-130 / ABU-100** office codes. None is replaced by this new source or assigned a resolved cause.
+
+The new memorandum narrows one uncertainty: the order number was expressly cited in this particular same-year audit context. The missing operative text/version, FAA implementation and case-specific routing still determine what applied to the target investigation. Do not infer a mandatory investigation deadline, a breach, a signed disposition or a delivered Commission correction from the audit citation.
+
+## A directly observed text-search limitation
+
+The initial PDF text-navigation pass found no matching 8000.1C or follow-up expression. The web reader's text search also found no 8000 match. Yet the citation and follow-up wording are visible on **physical p. 106**. The local extractor returns only **31 characters for p. 105** and **12 for p. 106**, substantially less than the visible memorandum bodies. Preserve both the extraction results and the visible source reading; the PDF was not OCR-repaired or overwritten.
+
+This is a reproducible limitation of these search representations, not evidence that the policy citation was absent, later inserted, concealed or substituted. The lesson for the remaining acquisition is specific: inspect the relevant source pages when an attached memorandum's body is not exposed by the text layer. A zero keyword hit cannot certify a missing record. No claim is made about every other page or search system.
+
+## What remains TODO, and the next discriminating records
+
+- **PD01:** actual corrected May 22, 2003 QFR, version/attachments, dispatch and recipient acknowledgment. A financial-audit memorandum is not the correction or receipt.
+- **PD02:** signed consideration/action/no-action determination, reasons, supporting record and dated notification. Agreement with 28 unrelated financial recommendations is not that decision.
+- **PD03:** case-specific response, investigation recommendation resolution, implementation and closure history. Investigation closure, recommendation resolution, implementation, correction delivery and personnel consideration remain distinct outcomes.
+- **PD04:** operative FAA 2900.1 text/amendments and completed issuance/office-history records, including the earlier Form 1320-6 route; DOT order version/chapter coverage and the actual CC-2006-085 routing/notice. The full 2006 financial-audit file or directive history may supply additional pointers, but is not assumed to contain the investigation's disposition.
+
+All five work-plan tracks and eighteen original-input requirements remain open. This new original-source acquisition is partial PD04 evidence, not completion of the work plan or a change to the user's research scope. No new claim of concealment, unlawful action, coordination or historical cause is made. The strongest limitation is that the demonstrated audit context and the target investigation are different records and potentially different procedures; only the missing source-specific policy and case record can establish their relationship.
+
+## Actual reading and preservation checks
+
+Six page images were read: physical **1, 6, 103, 104, 105 and 106**, rendered at **155 dpi**. They cover the report identity/foreword, financial-section context and complete two-page OIG memorandum. The remainder was used for text navigation only, not claimed visually read. No complete KPMG audit, whole-report factual review, OCR, native-signature authentication, case outcome test or scientific clock analysis was performed.
+
+[SOURCES.json](SOURCES.json) preserves the source/access/hash/page relationships; [OBSERVATIONS.json](OBSERVATIONS.json) gives exact source and report-line locators. [OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) retains PD01–PD04. [SOURCE-CHECKS.json](SOURCE-CHECKS.json) records entity/page/extraction checks, not independent validation of image readings, policy applicability or historical events. [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) is the exact additive research-note diff; earlier reports and every conflicting source value remain untouched.
+
+Only original research notes, source pins and verification code/results are published. Raw PDF/rasters/extractions, signatures, contact details, private correspondence, credentials and strategy are excluded. No mailbox access, agency/witness outreach, fee, new request/filing, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite occurred.
